From fe9c6fb67986f11028cc7a2961a68e1fb812dff9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 14:48:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix photo tap dead-click, decouple Dues/Dealers from period
 picker, add bar charts to every report
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The photo viewer returned null whenever there was no photo yet, so
tapping an empty avatar on a team member's profile did nothing visible
— it looked broken rather than "no photo". It now always opens the
sheet: a real photo with download/share, or a clear "no photo added
yet" empty state when there isn't one.

Dues and Dealers were being fetched in the same period-gated batch as
Orders and Item-wise sales, even though neither get_team_member_summary
nor get_team_member_dealers takes a date range at all — they're running
totals. Picking "Custom" and not yet filling both dates blanked out
Dues/Dealers too, for no reason tied to the period. Split into two
effects: Dues/Dealers load as soon as the profile is open, Orders/
Item-wise sales stay gated behind a ready date range.

Added a small bar chart to every report, reusing the existing plain
div-bar style already used for item-wise sales rather than pulling in
a charting library: top dealers by outstanding on Dues, an owner vs
granted-access split on Dealers, order value bucketed by day (or wider
buckets for long periods) on Orders, and a "top items by quantity"
caption on the existing item-wise sales bars.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GxWPdEf21EL6SvRpGBbX8q
